ask from the community. At this time, that is correct, yes. We're just

01:06:28.423 --> 01:06:31.953
looking for direction. Won't it need some to install water,

01:06:32.178 --> 01:06:35.839
like to get the spigot part of the water line on and some of those

01:06:35.871 --> 01:06:39.291
other things staff-wise? So it's just setup cost

01:06:39.644 --> 01:06:42.951
but not maintenance costs, correct? Yes.

01:06:43.161 --> 01:06:46.264
Okay. I actually am a huge supporter of this.

01:06:46.862 --> 01:06:50.256
There's places all over the state of Utah where Master

01:06:50.756 --> 01:06:54.168
Gardeners go and volunteer to Thanksgiving Point, Temple Square.

01:06:54.686 --> 01:06:58.404
They go and they help maintain a certain area that they're given

01:06:58.904 --> 01:07:02.318
responsibility for, and it's awesome. So like, I think this is the direction

01:07:02.818 --> 01:07:06.754
we want to head as a city. Well, and on

01:07:06.786 --> 01:07:09.984
this, like, something that I know has been thrown around out there is

01:07:10.178 --> 01:07:13.521
different classes, and what better place to have a gardening class and add a garden.

01:07:14.433 --> 01:07:16.110
It would give us a place to do that.

01:07:19.622 --> 01:07:22.825
Mayor? I just want to add one. I think my biggest

01:07:22.873 --> 01:07:26.545
concern with this idea over the years has just been the liability that it

01:07:26.593 --> 01:07:30.294
could potentially put the city into. And what I mean by that is we've talked

01:07:30.794 --> 01:07:34.760
a lot about in these corridors putting a lot of fruit trees in or doing

01:07:34.776 --> 01:07:38.580
these community gardens. And what if somebody goes out and sprays chemical

01:07:39.080 --> 01:07:43.199
application on something to treat for some bug that's there and then somebody picks

01:07:43.248 --> 01:07:46.779
the fruit and gets sick. And so that's

01:07:47.279 --> 01:07:50.166
my protective nature of the city to bring up these things. And I think that

01:07:50.666 --> 01:07:53.231
some of those things need to be mitigated as we work through this. And I

01:07:53.280 --> 01:07:56.297
think that we need some barriers or parameters to work through it

01:07:57.196 --> 01:08:00.005
and address some of those situations if we are gonna move forward with it,

01:08:00.583 --> 01:08:04.082
just to protect the city. Like a waiver, I understand

01:08:04.114 --> 01:08:08.255
that I could die from eating these peaches. I also think that the fence

01:08:08.432 --> 01:08:11.836
probably is, one that should happen sooner

01:08:11.964 --> 01:08:15.079
rather than later because— and we get a lock on

01:08:15.175 --> 01:08:19.222
the water spigot. And those— somebody

01:08:19.270 --> 01:08:23.316
asked the cost of the water. That is part of what that monthly maintenance fee

01:08:23.621 --> 01:08:27.378
for whoever is. They would basically rent a space. Like, say for instance,

01:08:27.411 --> 01:08:30.365
the box is a 4 by 8. They would rent a 4 by 4 or

01:08:30.865 --> 01:08:34.379
a 4 by 8. And so then those monthly costs would help

01:08:34.879 --> 01:08:38.183
pay for all of those My only thought is if

01:08:38.473 --> 01:08:42.069
we move forward with this, and I'm supportive as well, that we just

01:08:42.569 --> 01:08:46.244
have good materials, that we don't halfway do this where

01:08:46.744 --> 01:08:50.788
your 2x4s are rotting out in 2 years. I mean, I think this

01:08:50.900 --> 01:08:54.352
is a social experiment. They don't own the boxes, they don't

01:08:54.433 --> 01:08:58.142
own the material, the equipment. It's not their own property. And when it's

01:08:58.642 --> 01:09:00.534
not yours, you tend to just let things dilapidate. I think that's a good point.

01:09:00.600 --> 01:09:04.065
So I think if we move forward, that the

01:09:04.565 --> 01:09:08.235
materials would need to be good quality, that can be durable,

01:09:08.556 --> 01:09:12.134
last a long time, like a playground. You just build it

01:09:12.634 --> 01:09:15.631
to last. Well, and I fully support that, and that can get a little more

01:09:16.131 --> 01:09:19.770
costly, of course, but that is why, I mean, if the city was

01:09:19.866 --> 01:09:23.331
open to it, we could have a sponsor-a-bed program or something like

01:09:23.831 --> 01:09:28.465
that where different people or businesses could donate money or They

01:09:28.965 --> 01:09:32.541
could donate the bud for us, and that would be

01:09:33.041 --> 01:09:35.525
a way to make sure it was done the right way. See, and I like

01:09:36.025 --> 01:09:38.494
that idea because it could help people that maybe couldn't afford to pay the maintenance

01:09:38.994 --> 01:09:42.313
fee, but they could seek sponsorships. But so what I'm hearing, or what I'm understanding,

01:09:42.345 --> 01:09:45.234
and maybe you can correct me, it sounds like there's support,

01:09:45.860 --> 01:09:49.663
but we need maybe some— I don't

01:09:50.163 --> 01:09:52.695
know if I want to call it a contract. We need some guardrails or some

01:09:53.195 --> 01:09:56.696
agreements, if you will, LOI, whatever Mechanism that says

01:09:56.793 --> 01:10:00.333
here's the the property, here's who the manager

01:10:00.382 --> 01:10:03.576
is at this time, and and here's how it's going to operate. For instance,

01:10:05.155 --> 01:10:09.051
the liability question on the sprays that if there's spray used

01:10:09.084 --> 01:10:12.320
that number one has to be approved by the city first. You can't spray without,

01:10:13.930 --> 01:10:17.817
and then secondly posting a sign or something that says

01:10:17.849 --> 01:10:21.306
that this has been sprayed, or you know there's some kind of. Notice, you know,

01:10:21.322 --> 01:10:23.925
I'm just giving an example. So go ahead. Yeah,

01:10:24.184 --> 01:10:27.838
I'll share some thoughts. I'm probably gonna be the one who's the outsider on

01:10:27.951 --> 01:10:31.622
this a little bit. I don't think this is a good idea for the city

01:10:32.122 --> 01:10:35.716
to get involved in this. And so my

01:10:36.216 --> 01:10:39.348
approach to it would be to look for corporate sponsorship, to find

01:10:39.848 --> 01:10:42.128
a way to put it. I think the city could donate the land, or at

01:10:42.628 --> 01:10:46.060
least dedicate the land and make the water accessible. But I don't think the city

01:10:46.092 --> 01:10:49.942
should take responsibility of managing it, or playing any part of it.

01:10:50.439 --> 01:10:53.715
I think if the community wants to see it be successful, that we

01:10:54.215 --> 01:10:58.291
should go seek some private funding to put in the original beds, and then

01:10:58.791 --> 01:11:01.759
let the city dedicate the space for that to happen, and let those who wanna

01:11:02.259 --> 01:11:05.356
come participate pay the few dollars that you're talking about to be able to

01:11:05.856 --> 01:11:09.113
do that. And Jen, I don't know where you're gonna find your time. I mean,

01:11:09.129 --> 01:11:12.084
I know how busy you are. I'm grateful that you're willing to teach that to

01:11:12.100 --> 01:11:15.697
our residents, and I think that it, I think in concept I really

01:11:15.729 --> 01:11:20.034
enjoy it. I just don't think it's something the city should be funding and

01:11:20.547 --> 01:11:23.567
being held responsible for. So I think that is the thing,

01:11:23.599 --> 01:11:26.651
is it's on city land, and that's why I wanted the guardrails. There is no

01:11:26.876 --> 01:11:30.281
funds asked and no staff time, but the land is there. So like,

01:11:30.345 --> 01:11:33.557
that's why I said I think we need the sign that says that,

01:11:33.782 --> 01:11:37.268
you know, it's been sprayed, or— But who's going to take that,

01:11:37.284 --> 01:11:39.339
Mayor? I mean, and who's going to monitor it? Are we going to have a

01:11:39.839 --> 01:11:43.017
staff member that goes by and watches this every— I mean, those are the problems

01:11:43.517 --> 01:11:46.950
that I think these types of things cause, or at

01:11:47.450 --> 01:11:50.820
least the concerns from a liability standpoint. I mean, if I'm a private business owner

01:11:51.320 --> 01:11:53.758
and you're asking to come do this on my property, I have all the same

01:11:53.855 --> 01:11:57.130
concerns that I have as a member of the city council for the city.

01:11:58.110 --> 01:12:01.739
I mean, there'd have to be some indemnification from my perspective of

01:12:01.883 --> 01:12:05.271
anybody who participates in it or consumes anything that's grown in

01:12:05.771 --> 01:12:08.846
it. The city needs some indemnification from my perspective.

01:12:08.942 --> 01:12:12.084
There's just too many unknowns in that.

01:12:12.164 --> 01:12:15.418
That's problematic for me as someone who looks out for some of

01:12:15.450 --> 01:12:18.416
those things in my own private life, in my own business.

01:12:19.282 --> 01:12:22.616
The buck always stops with me. If you can find someone

01:12:23.116 --> 01:12:26.110
to sponsor, I'll sponsor a bed. I'll just say that out loud and on the

01:12:26.610 --> 01:12:29.797
public record. I'll be happy to sponsor a bed at the $200 or whatever

01:12:30.297 --> 01:12:33.966
you need, but I think we We can find a way to do that through

01:12:34.466 --> 01:12:38.135
our business partners rather than trying to

01:12:38.296 --> 01:12:41.888
put that on the city. And only if we can find a path forward with

01:12:42.388 --> 01:12:45.880
our attorney to find some way to indemnify the city against some

01:12:46.153 --> 01:12:50.322
potential future loss. I would just kind

01:12:50.822 --> 01:12:55.550
of ask too, with the concerns about liability, we have park

01:12:56.050 --> 01:13:00.057
equipment that people play on and could get hurt at. How do we

01:13:00.106 --> 01:13:03.959
indemnify ourselves with that? There's signage, play at your own risk,

01:13:04.023 --> 01:13:07.652
those kinds of things. So I feel like the way

01:13:07.716 --> 01:13:11.072
that we create some of the guardrails that you're talking about,

01:13:11.088 --> 01:13:14.846
because us doing it as a city versus a private business doing

01:13:14.862 --> 01:13:18.073
it, there's a lot different liabilities that you

01:13:18.573 --> 01:13:21.991
have to take on as a business because the buck stops

01:13:22.491 --> 01:13:25.875
with you. But as a city, it's to me it's like. Playground equipment in a

01:13:26.375 --> 01:13:30.163
lot of ways. So I just maybe wanted to jump in there really

01:13:30.663 --> 01:13:34.046
quickly. Um, as far as things like park equipment

01:13:34.546 --> 01:13:37.257
and all that kind of thing, anybody can sue anybody for any reason, and the

01:13:37.757 --> 01:13:40.533
city could be sued at any time. And that's why we have insurance with the

01:13:41.033 --> 01:13:44.730
trust. We mitigate the impact of that by having policies

01:13:44.762 --> 01:13:47.928
and procedures in place, by having good record keeping that says this is

01:13:47.976 --> 01:13:51.455
how we're maintaining this, and all that type of I think what I'm hearing from

01:13:52.113 --> 01:13:55.613
various groups, there are various members of the council

01:13:55.645 --> 01:13:59.017
here, is that the word guardrails or

01:13:59.517 --> 01:14:03.433
the world or the rules or how it's going to be administered— did

01:14:03.933 --> 01:14:07.479
the city act prudently? Did we put the right rules in place?

01:14:07.543 --> 01:14:10.610
