01:43:10.681 --> 01:43:14.313
And— Yeah, we have Jason Ayu.

01:43:15.098 --> 01:43:15.769
Jason Ayu.

01:43:23.752 --> 01:43:27.156
You're good now. Okay. Good evening, Mayor, Council.

01:43:27.702 --> 01:43:31.219
My name is Jason Ayew. My wife and I, my wife Joanne and I,

01:43:31.235 --> 01:43:34.109
have been here for 26 years in Eagle Mountain. This is our home, this is

01:43:34.609 --> 01:43:37.818
our community, and we're excited to be able to discuss item

01:43:38.318 --> 01:43:41.912
12A, which is a plat. And on that plat, you're gonna hear about our site

01:43:42.412 --> 01:43:45.862
plan for a school that we propose. It's a charter school called Ripple Academy.

01:43:47.596 --> 01:43:51.282
Having my children have born

01:43:51.782 --> 01:43:55.047
and raised here in Eagle Mountain and have been great products of the public school

01:43:55.063 --> 01:43:59.038
system. One thing that I've learned from my own 2 children is that

01:43:59.070 --> 01:44:02.595
both, even though living in the same home, they both have 2 completely different

01:44:03.095 --> 01:44:07.258
learning styles. And my son Chaz thrived really well in a traditional

01:44:07.579 --> 01:44:11.617
learning, moved on and went to college, graduated from college. My daughter Zion,

01:44:11.729 --> 01:44:15.017
not so much. She really struggle with the traditional learning style. And so

01:44:15.081 --> 01:44:18.355
Ripple Academy is a life-based learning

01:44:18.387 --> 01:44:21.629
model that, you know, thinking about as we develop this school,

01:44:21.757 --> 01:44:25.256
it really would've been fantastic for my daughter Zion

01:44:26.074 --> 01:44:29.188
to be in this school. But we can't go backwards, we can only move forward.

01:44:30.247 --> 01:44:33.473
And, you know, as we put some initial interest out

01:44:33.973 --> 01:44:38.175
there, our school proposes hopefully will be open by next August 2027

01:44:38.207 --> 01:44:41.570
if everything goes well, knock on wood. But we've already had over 300

01:44:42.070 --> 01:44:46.023
members, 300 members of Eagle Mountain that have expressed interest into that

01:44:46.410 --> 01:44:49.814
learning-based model of Ripple Academy. And so we just want to put

01:44:50.314 --> 01:44:53.236
a name and a face in front of you as you— I'm sure you'll hear

01:44:53.268 --> 01:44:56.738
from us many times forward, but thank you for your time and hopefully we

01:44:57.238 --> 01:45:00.209
appreciate your support in getting our site plan approved. So thank you.

01:45:03.036 --> 01:45:03.523
Anthony Wood.

01:45:14.716 --> 01:45:17.933
How's it going? I put my comment

01:45:18.433 --> 01:45:21.806
down under item 16, but it was— it's not really directed towards

01:45:21.856 --> 01:45:25.737
that. Essentially, I wanted to say thank

01:45:25.786 --> 01:45:30.412
you guys. Thank you for, you know, listening to us and

01:45:30.912 --> 01:45:34.721
working together with residents. In regards to that truth in taxation, we did. I know

01:45:34.785 --> 01:45:37.384
you guys were facing a lot of varying degrees of criticism,

01:45:38.337 --> 01:45:40.387
and much of it seemed to be pretty distasteful.

01:45:43.101 --> 01:45:46.620
I know you guys had a lot of late nights and very long conversations

01:45:47.641 --> 01:45:49.960
helping everyone figure it out and get the information out there.

01:45:52.301 --> 01:45:55.809
I appreciate we were able to come together and come to a very reasonable number.

01:45:56.747 --> 01:45:58.445
I found myself talking to a lot of residents.

01:45:59.891 --> 01:46:03.826
Many of them were blaming council members for all of the truth in taxation

01:46:03.875 --> 01:46:08.677
stuff. And I found myself telling them a story and

01:46:09.113 --> 01:46:11.808
that they needed to realize that they were slightly accountable as well.

01:46:13.460 --> 01:46:17.094
Now, that story was essentially just imagine that your family

01:46:18.596 --> 01:46:22.135
is the city. You know, you're the city council. Your spouse

01:46:22.411 --> 01:46:25.094
is the mayor. Your kids are the residents.

01:46:27.351 --> 01:46:30.095
You know, your family is pregnant, you have another kid on the way,

01:46:31.282 --> 01:46:34.475
and you start saving up for a new car because you need one.

01:46:35.309 --> 01:46:38.357
You know, after a few doctor visits, you find out you're having triplets,

01:46:38.582 --> 01:46:41.694
and now that car is not going to do. You need a minivan.

01:46:41.903 --> 01:46:44.823
It's going to cost a lot more money. You go to your family, you tell

01:46:45.323 --> 01:46:48.497
them like, hey, I'm going to cut back on your allowances because we need

01:46:48.997 --> 01:46:50.919
to finance this vehicle we can't quite afford, but we need it now.

01:46:52.180 --> 01:46:56.094
No. You hear crickets. You come back a couple

01:46:56.594 --> 01:46:59.548
days later, you tell them again. Again, no response. Crickets.

01:47:01.146 --> 01:47:04.149
Now, what I was telling everyone is that, you know,

01:47:04.359 --> 01:47:07.475
they get all mad when they find out that their allowances were cut.

01:47:08.832 --> 01:47:10.979
You know, what are you doing? What are you doing? You know, you're cutting my

01:47:11.479 --> 01:47:13.930
allowance back. You know, oh, we had to get that van. Well,

01:47:15.331 --> 01:47:18.148
they'll start replying with like, we didn't need that van. Who told you we needed

01:47:18.648 --> 01:47:20.274
that? Like, we don't need it. It's too expensive. where are you putting the money?

01:47:20.339 --> 01:47:23.631
We could have done something different. You know, all those crickets during the first

01:47:24.131 --> 01:47:27.699
conversations were us residents not coming to the first few meetings and discussing

01:47:28.199 --> 01:47:31.993
everything and figuring it all out. Ultimately,

01:47:33.006 --> 01:47:36.557
I was telling them that if you want to know what's going on, or,

01:47:37.248 --> 01:47:40.551
you know, if you want to complain and have some value behind it, you need

01:47:41.051 --> 01:47:43.458
to come to the meetings and listen and know what's going on.

01:47:44.287 --> 01:47:47.964
I heard some residents talking about how 30 seconds

01:47:47.997 --> 01:47:51.637
remaining. Some residents were complaining about

01:47:52.137 --> 01:47:54.272
like, oh, you know, we didn't discuss this. I want to know this, I want

01:47:54.772 --> 01:47:57.409
to know this. And I was literally sending them dates of when we were having

01:47:57.441 --> 01:48:00.850
council meetings in the past where you guys covered that. And I was sending them

01:48:01.235 --> 01:48:04.499
video clips from those meetings.

01:48:04.547 --> 01:48:08.084
And it's like, they discussed it, you weren't there. I just wanted to say thank

01:48:08.584 --> 01:48:08.646
you though, so.

01:48:13.604 --> 01:48:17.329
All right, that's everybody that's turned in a form. Is there anybody that

01:48:17.939 --> 01:48:20.316
did not get an opportunity that would like to speak at this time?

01:48:21.600 --> 01:48:25.389
Seeing no one, we will close the public comment period

01:48:25.889 --> 01:48:28.745
at 7:13 and bring it back to the council. And,

01:48:28.826 --> 01:48:32.615
uh, for this time has been set aside for them to make comments

01:48:33.115 --> 01:48:35.762
and address the public. We'll start with Councilmember Clark.

01:48:37.320 --> 01:48:39.921
Thank you, Mayor, and thank you for your thoughts.

01:48:40.145 --> 01:48:43.822
Ironically, I have a set of twins, and we only had one

01:48:43.935 --> 01:48:47.837
kid when we found out we were having them, and we had to move

01:48:47.869 --> 01:48:51.241
to a minivan too, and it was a major life change. It,

01:48:51.385 --> 01:48:55.174
like, we didn't fit in the car that we had anymore, and it

01:48:55.191 --> 01:48:58.771
was a pretty big deal. So, like, I really got

01:48:59.271 --> 01:49:01.308
the visual of what you shared. Thank you.

01:49:03.508 --> 01:49:06.818
I have to remind myself when people get mad

01:49:07.318 --> 01:49:10.723
at me or call me something on Facebook that the only difference between

01:49:10.755 --> 01:49:14.338
me and the people who are saying what they're saying on Facebook is information.

01:49:15.077 --> 01:49:18.644
And we're working hard to improve what we do as far

01:49:19.144 --> 01:49:22.742
as information goes and getting that information out to you. And we're,

01:49:22.967 --> 01:49:26.405
we're patient with our residents because we know what it feels like to be

01:49:26.486 --> 01:49:29.523
angry about something or confused. Or afraid.

01:49:30.454 --> 01:49:33.748
So give us, give us a

01:49:34.248 --> 01:49:37.990
little bit of grace as we work through finding out information about how

01:49:38.490 --> 01:49:41.273
to get you information. One of the things that we discussed during our work session

01:49:41.305 --> 01:49:44.864
today was our normal community survey that we do

01:49:45.364 --> 01:49:48.948
each year, and one of the questions that we talked about was finding

01:49:48.981 --> 01:49:51.957
out from our residents what's the best way to communicate with you,

01:49:52.359 --> 01:49:56.430
what mode of communication is going to actually serve

01:49:56.930 --> 01:50:01.250
serve you the best. And I think that attention to detail is something that gets

01:50:01.750 --> 01:50:05.026
missed by people who aren't here sitting

01:50:05.059 --> 01:50:08.381
up on the dais. But we want you to know that we,

01:50:09.755 --> 01:50:13.535
we really do want you to be a part of the process. We believe in

01:50:14.035 --> 01:50:16.862
your ability to help us make decisions, and we're grateful that you're here.

01:50:18.341 --> 01:50:21.587
And I just want to say too how grateful I am for our staff.

01:50:22.136 --> 01:50:26.166
They put in countless hours. I know our recorder's office had

01:50:26.666 --> 01:50:29.273
to get a packet ready, then they had to get a bunch of other stuff

01:50:29.338 --> 01:50:33.015
ready and meet deadlines. And they're not the only ones

01:50:33.047 --> 01:50:36.090
that are just busting their tails to make things go in our city.

01:50:36.976 --> 01:50:39.793
And I just am super grateful. We wouldn't be able to be who we are

01:50:40.293 --> 01:50:40.997
without you guys. So thank you.

01:50:44.325 --> 01:50:47.708
Thank you, Mayor. Yeah, thank you, Mr. Wood. I appreciate your comments.

01:50:48.898 --> 01:50:51.403
We've taken it on the chin for a few weeks, and it's nice to hear

01:50:51.903 --> 01:50:55.449
somebody that actually appreciates what we do. Whether we get it right or wrong,

01:50:56.300 --> 01:50:59.559
we know that we do both. I mean, I recognize

01:50:59.656 --> 01:51:03.092
that, at least I get it that way. Sometimes I get it wrong,

01:51:04.007 --> 01:51:07.861
and hopefully that's a minor amount of the time, and more

01:51:08.361 --> 01:51:11.120
often than not, we make good decisions. I call them SUDs,

01:51:11.457 --> 01:51:15.419
seemingly unimportant decisions, and we make Lots of them. And I

01:51:15.500 --> 01:51:19.089
think that the more that we can make in a positive manner that

01:51:19.138 --> 01:51:22.453
bring positive results, that ultimately those benefits and

01:51:22.953 --> 01:51:26.941
blessings will come up and they show up on our doorstep. So seemingly unimportant

01:51:27.441 --> 01:51:30.877
decisions that we make daily, weekly, yearly as we sit

01:51:31.377 --> 01:51:34.348
here and have the opportunity to make those decisions on your behalf.

01:51:34.479 --> 01:51:38.130
So thank you for your words. Welcome to all

01:51:38.198 --> 01:51:41.967
of you that are here. It's good to see some smiling faces. Mr. Ayoub,

01:51:41.983 --> 01:51:44.052
you don't know me, but I know your dad pretty well.

01:51:45.977 --> 01:51:49.355
And what an awesome man your father

01:51:50.529 --> 01:51:53.558
is. And so thank you for being— I didn't know that you're a member of

01:51:54.058 --> 01:51:57.747
our community, so that makes me happy. I've only been here 22 years,

01:51:57.860 --> 01:52:00.887
not 26. So you got me beat there.

01:52:01.674 --> 01:52:04.774
And then I want to just— I guess I want to make this point.

01:52:05.062 --> 01:52:07.872
And I know that the council members know this. I met with the seniors today,

01:52:08.177 --> 01:52:11.693
the senior citizens. I'm the liaison for the city with the senior citizens from

01:52:11.709 --> 01:52:14.952
the city council, and they expressed some concerns

01:52:15.452 --> 01:52:18.917
and some issues that they're having that are not unlike what our staff members deal

01:52:19.014 --> 01:52:22.738
with. They need more room. They've got more members

01:52:23.238 --> 01:52:26.142
of their community that want to come and they want to participate in their building.

01:52:26.656 --> 01:52:30.188
We added a building there 2 years ago, 3 years ago.

01:52:30.333 --> 01:52:33.287
Was it last year? Last year. It's— and they've outgrown it already. And it was

01:52:33.303 --> 01:52:35.872
just a trailer. It's just a Connex. It's an extra, right?

01:52:36.835 --> 01:52:40.303
What do they call them at the school? A pod of some portable of

01:52:40.803 --> 01:52:44.398
some sort. And we were fortunate that we had some federal funds that allowed

01:52:44.898 --> 01:52:47.384
us to do that. Didn't come out of our taxpayer dollars, at least locally.

01:52:47.449 --> 01:52:51.527
It came out of some federal funds. And so I'm asking the council to consider

01:52:51.607 --> 01:52:55.172
perhaps directing some of those CBDG funds in that direction towards

01:52:55.220 --> 01:52:58.816
them. But it also underlines at least a major concern

01:52:58.913 --> 01:53:02.325
that I have is For our staff members, we're looking at hiring some new people.

01:53:04.080 --> 01:53:07.592
For every person we hire, we probably need 3 that we should be hiring.

01:53:08.197 --> 01:53:10.902
And for every person that we hire, that's just,

01:53:11.480 --> 01:53:14.661
that's just 10 more people that are having to work out of closets or from

01:53:14.709 --> 01:53:18.389
home or remotely. And I don't think our citizens really see that

01:53:18.889 --> 01:53:22.098
impact, but I'm, I've been here long enough now that I'm, I'm seeing that and

01:53:22.988 --> 01:53:25.891
we just lose efficiencies when we have to function that way. So I hope that

01:53:26.391 --> 01:53:29.616
you'll bear with us as we make many hard decisions. We're talking about a sewer

01:53:30.116 --> 01:53:33.630
treatment plant, huge bond. But if you want that

01:53:34.130 --> 01:53:35.926
stuff to go where it's supposed to do, we have to make the right decisions,

01:53:36.183 --> 01:53:39.635
right? So I just, I want to express my love and

01:53:39.731 --> 01:53:43.167
my gratitude to each of you for allowing me the

01:53:43.247 --> 01:53:46.747
opportunity to serve. I'm nothing special.

01:53:47.101 --> 01:53:51.387
I don't know a whole lot, and I've learned even more having

01:53:51.517 --> 01:53:54.928
out here, but what I can promise you is that every decision

01:53:55.009 --> 01:53:59.553
that I make, I will always do it—

01:53:59.763 --> 01:54:03.410
I will always make it asking this question: What's in the best interest

01:54:03.910 --> 01:54:07.407
of the people who are members of my community, myself, my family,

01:54:07.520 --> 01:54:10.115
and you who are here in attendance tonight? So thank you.

01:54:13.434 --> 01:54:15.278
Welcome, everybody. It's great to have you. Go Cougs.

01:54:17.850 --> 01:54:20.463
Thank you. Wow, yeah, this last,

01:54:20.832 --> 01:54:23.750
last month or so has been quite, quite a month for us up here.

01:54:24.456 --> 01:54:27.807
And I've thought about a lot of things, learned a lot from residents

01:54:28.307 --> 01:54:31.832
and shared a lot in return. And I just wanted to make a couple comments.

01:54:33.179 --> 01:54:36.883
You know, when we communicate with one another, you can

01:54:37.383 --> 01:54:40.571
either assume ill intent from the beginning and begin your relationship that way, or you

01:54:40.635 --> 01:54:43.794
can assume good intent and begin it that

01:54:44.294 --> 01:54:47.855
way and then make decisions from there. A quote that I like, great minds discuss

01:54:48.355 --> 01:54:51.805
ideas, average minds discuss events, and small minds discuss people.

01:54:51.949 --> 01:54:55.819
Well, when it came to the tax discussions, some people kept

01:54:56.319 --> 01:54:58.918
it at the idea level, and ideas were going back and forth.

01:54:59.672 --> 01:55:03.044
Then at the end of the day, after ideas were discussed, people could say,

01:55:03.108 --> 01:55:06.336
well, I agree with that approach, or I don't agree with that approach, but it

01:55:06.836 --> 01:55:10.109
didn't get personal. It was just, I have a different managerial style or a different

01:55:10.609 --> 01:55:14.117
vision. And there's no animosity in that. But I found there were

01:55:14.617 --> 01:55:18.011
a lot of people that stayed down at the people level instead of discussing

01:55:18.107 --> 01:55:22.033
ideas level, and they just wanted to attack character and attack,

01:55:23.154 --> 01:55:26.391
you know, just attack and assume ill intent.

01:55:26.456 --> 01:55:30.366
And I don't think that's safe for a marriage. And when

01:55:30.866 --> 01:55:34.596
you have a marriage companionship, you know, you should hopefully assume good intent and that

01:55:34.868 --> 01:55:38.049
if there's been a miscommunication, it's usually been There's been a miscommunication,

01:55:39.612 --> 01:55:42.836
but I'm grateful for the for the residents that that kept

01:55:43.336 --> 01:55:46.897
the discussion on ideas because when that happened, solutions came

01:55:46.945 --> 01:55:50.264
out and bridge building came out. And I think that's a lot where we

01:55:50.392 --> 01:55:54.212
where we need to keep keep our discussions at the idea at the idea

01:55:54.616 --> 01:55:57.883
stage instead of it attacking character stage.

01:55:58.562 --> 01:56:02.379
And I recognize as public officials we're going to get you

01:56:02.879 --> 01:56:05.380
know we're going to get some of the character attacks and that that's going to

01:56:05.880 --> 01:56:09.400
happen and. I would just invite people to come meet with us first and then

01:56:09.416 --> 01:56:12.717
make a decision if you want to about our character after you come actually meet

01:56:13.217 --> 01:56:16.180
with us. We live in your same neighborhoods. We ride the same, drive on the

01:56:16.680 --> 01:56:19.928
same roads, go to the same schools, cheer for the same Cedar Valley High School

01:56:20.428 --> 01:56:23.758
football team, and we're in the stands with you. Just come say hi to

01:56:23.774 --> 01:56:27.460
us. Come meet us. I homeschool my kids, and then

01:56:27.960 --> 01:56:31.292
my kids have done some various things with the public school as well, and I

01:56:31.792 --> 01:56:35.408
love the diverse opportunities for learning because you're right,

01:56:35.488 --> 01:56:39.115
all, you know, our minds don't, you know, all think

01:56:39.615 --> 01:56:42.245
the same way and we do need different ways to be able to learn and

01:56:42.745 --> 01:56:46.210
grow. So I'm excited to have the discussion a little bit later about

01:56:46.274 --> 01:56:49.597
that school you have going in. Thanks for bringing that. And that,

01:56:49.950 --> 01:56:53.176
again, that's the idea phase, right? The ideas that bring

01:56:53.676 --> 01:56:57.815
solutions. That's more what we need. We need more ideas and we're better

01:56:58.315 --> 01:57:01.058
together when we can share ideas with one another. So Thanks for your patience with

01:57:01.106 --> 01:57:04.767
us as we work through this process. I actually gained

01:57:04.944 --> 01:57:08.059
more friends from this than I probably gained maybe some enemies as well,

01:57:08.797 --> 01:57:12.265
but I don't consider them enemies, and they might consider me an enemy.

01:57:12.587 --> 01:57:15.284
But I met some people I didn't know before that I'm like, wow, I have

01:57:15.332 --> 01:57:18.014
much respect for, gained greater respect for in this process.

01:57:19.170 --> 01:57:21.241
And so I'm grateful for the people that reached out and took the time to

01:57:21.741 --> 01:57:25.400
actually get to know us, have legitimate discussions that moved

01:57:25.520 --> 01:57:26.322
the city forward.

01:57:29.860 --> 01:57:32.286
Yeah, thank you, Anthony, for making that comment.

01:57:33.989 --> 01:57:37.749
I had a coworker yesterday, she came to my office and she said,

01:57:37.765 --> 01:57:41.165
you're famous. I was like, really? She said,

01:57:41.213 --> 01:57:43.991
yeah, my daughter's been following everything on your city on TikTok.

01:57:45.186 --> 01:57:47.786
Like, that's not how I wanted to get famous,

01:57:49.140 --> 01:57:52.864
but that's okay. Everybody now in America knows

01:57:52.995 --> 01:57:54.682
about property taxes in Eagle Mountain.

01:57:57.353 --> 01:58:00.629
You know, I look at all the positives that have come from this.

01:58:00.839 --> 01:58:04.276
Tonight we're proposing code that would not have existed

01:58:04.793 --> 01:58:07.186
had we not had an active conversation in the city.

01:58:07.931 --> 01:58:11.396
We'll hopefully be putting in place a safety fund that

01:58:11.428 --> 01:58:15.686
when you pay your property tax, 100% of

01:58:16.572 --> 01:58:20.297
That will go into a safety fund segregated from sales tax. That's something

01:58:20.345 --> 01:58:23.444
that didn't— has never existed, as far as I know, in our city.

01:58:23.958 --> 01:58:28.181
We'll be creating, hopefully, if it passes, a rebalancing

01:58:28.920 --> 01:58:33.094
mechanism for city councils to not just kick the can down the road, you know,

01:58:33.110 --> 01:58:36.434
to have some kind of mechanism. Do we need to save up for a car?

01:58:37.125 --> 01:58:40.834
Do we need to consider that we are having triplets,

01:58:40.898 --> 01:58:44.830
and how do we plan for that? We're also

01:58:45.330 --> 01:58:49.260
going to be working on a budget in brief, a very simple 10-page

01:58:49.760 --> 01:58:53.384
document that is at an 18-year-old level. Somebody who can vote

01:58:53.657 --> 01:58:57.268
can read it and understand what's happening in the budget

01:58:57.768 --> 01:59:00.734
for the next year. So there's a lot of positive things I think that came

01:59:00.782 --> 01:59:04.329
from it. There's some negative things. There are certainly things that we've learned and things

01:59:04.829 --> 01:59:08.036
that we'll work on and improve next go-round. So I look at

01:59:08.536 --> 01:59:10.891
it and I think There are a lot of positive things that have come from

01:59:10.939 --> 01:59:14.444
it. And I'm just grateful. I think the one thing

01:59:14.540 --> 01:59:18.009
that we all have in common is we all love Eagle

01:59:18.509 --> 01:59:23.375
Mountain and we all want what's best. And sometimes that's gonna be crossing

01:59:23.423 --> 01:59:26.846
swords and sharpening our swords. But I, you know, I love what Craig's

01:59:27.346 --> 01:59:31.041
comment was. If we can focus on the ideas and

01:59:31.073 --> 01:59:34.507
come together with the best ideas, that's a huge

01:59:35.007 --> 01:59:38.670
positive. Thank you. So anyways, I'm just grateful. I'm grateful for the

01:59:39.170 --> 01:59:41.607
residents. I'm grateful for the process. It has been difficult,

01:59:42.615 --> 01:59:45.569
but I'm thankful for where we're landed.

01:59:48.120 --> 01:59:51.791
All right, thank you. Appreciate the comments. And just add that, yeah, I too

01:59:53.128 --> 01:59:56.575
love the things that we've learned. I look around

01:59:56.623 --> 01:59:59.549
and I think of all the really, really smart people, and one of them might

02:00:00.049 --> 02:00:02.660
be Scott Hazard. Smartest guys I know in the city.

02:00:03.270 --> 02:00:06.210
And when I was able to talk to him about some of the things that

02:00:06.710 --> 02:00:08.989
we were working on, he says, well, I didn't know that. I'm like, I knew

02:00:09.489 --> 02:00:13.010
something that Scott didn't know? That was like floored me, right? So it was,

02:00:13.510 --> 02:00:16.330
uh, it was definitely a learning experience, and especially with people that I really look

02:00:16.830 --> 02:00:19.770
up to, uh, to be able to do that. I also,

02:00:20.270 --> 02:00:23.730
uh, did get the opportunity to live next to the Ayus, and I really appreciate

02:00:24.230 --> 02:00:27.730
their ideas, uh, although I'm not going to admit whether it was my brother or

02:00:28.230 --> 02:00:31.499
not that might put a U in your front yard or not. I don't know

02:00:31.579 --> 02:00:35.323
anything about that, but I know that he also got one, so it might

02:00:35.823 --> 02:00:39.758
not have been him. But no, it's super fun to be neighbors. You're actually—

02:00:40.015 --> 02:00:42.442
you didn't know this, but on the other side of the hill, your backyards almost

02:00:42.942 --> 02:00:47.278
touch. So just on the other side of the hill. But the— yeah,

02:00:47.889 --> 02:00:51.456
it's super fun to see everybody come with their ideas. And I

02:00:51.665 --> 02:00:55.409
love the public when they get to come out and I thought Melissa

02:00:55.441 --> 02:00:58.734
would say it. I'm actually disappointed. When people come and yell at

02:00:59.234 --> 02:01:02.540
us like that, it's just people caring loudly, right? Isn't that the show from

02:01:03.392 --> 02:01:05.624
Parks and Rec, right? I just hear people caring loudly.

02:01:06.861 --> 02:01:10.443
So no, it's super fun. So thanks for all your input. I was

02:01:10.475 --> 02:01:13.752
gonna add the last few, last month has been a

02:01:14.252 --> 02:01:18.554
whirlwind, but we had the opportunity to go spend some time saving

02:01:18.651 --> 02:01:22.626
the city a lot of money. I think, over the years. And last week,

02:01:23.012 --> 02:01:26.314
me and a couple of staffers went back to New York and

02:01:26.814 --> 02:01:30.670
was able to help improve our bond rating. Just the work

02:01:31.155 --> 02:01:35.198
that was done there and the things that our staff does and our consultants,

02:01:35.263 --> 02:01:38.917
we had Laura Lewis with us, and it's just amazing. And then

02:01:39.417 --> 02:01:42.660
the people that were here trying to meet deadlines on,

02:01:42.951 --> 02:01:46.755
with the county and getting agendas ready. Thank you. And our attorneys

02:01:46.771 --> 02:01:48.942
reviewing documents and just the planning staff.

02:01:51.521 --> 02:01:55.634
Everybody was just, it has been a whirlwind. And so grateful

02:01:56.134 --> 02:01:59.440
for all the work that we're getting done and even constrained that we're

02:01:59.940 --> 02:02:03.780
able to really, really move the needle, I feel like, and do some cool things

02:02:03.878 --> 02:02:06.906
and hopefully save a lot of money and be able to keep that budget lean.

02:02:08.095 --> 02:02:11.588
So with that, I think we'll get started. And I know

02:02:12.088 --> 02:02:15.650
the first item We talked about in the, the work session, the consent agenda item

02:02:15.746 --> 02:02:18.651
12A might get moved to the— Yep.

02:02:19.614 --> 02:02:22.744
Would you accept a motion, Mayor? Yes, sir. Yes, ma'am. Mayor, I move

02:02:23.244 --> 02:02:26.547
that the City Council approve the consent agenda, removing item 12A

02:02:27.061 --> 02:02:30.704
from the consent agenda and placing it on the scheduled items

02:02:32.149 --> 02:02:35.503
section of the agenda. Second. Okay, we have

02:02:36.003 --> 02:02:39.733
a motion by Councilmember Clark and a second by Councilmember Wright. And we'll

02:02:40.233 --> 02:02:44.088
start the vote with Councilmember Hewish. Yes. Councilmember Clark.

02:02:44.168 --> 02:02:46.717
Yes. Councilmember Wright. Yes. Councilmember Whiting.

02:02:48.873 --> 02:02:51.904
Yes. Just, I just wanted to double-check. Councilmember Wood never, he did not join,

02:02:51.953 --> 02:02:54.741
right? Okay. Just making sure I didn't miss a vote.

02:02:56.958 --> 02:03:00.791
That passes 4 to 0. And we'll go right to

02:03:01.018 --> 02:03:04.075
item 12A, the Gateway Park.

02:03:04.841 --> 02:03:07.626
And I know, Steven, turn it to you.

02:03:10.243 --> 02:03:11.308
All right. Thank you.

02:03:17.019 --> 02:03:19.568
Do you have a screen coming?

02:03:21.770 --> 02:03:22.696
I'm patient this time.

02:03:26.323 --> 02:03:29.367
All right.

02:03:31.892 --> 02:03:34.459
Okay. Yeah, it seems like some of you are familiar with this. That's why it's

02:03:34.959 --> 02:03:38.543
been pulled off the agenda. This is a preliminary plat. Applications kind of come through

02:03:39.318 --> 02:03:43.264
quickly in attempts to help the proposed school to meet deadlines that

02:03:43.764 --> 02:03:47.193
they have to get this open when they want to. So the property

02:03:47.209 --> 02:03:51.320
we're dealing with is near the intersection of Mount Airy Drive

02:03:51.562 --> 02:03:55.184
and Corby Ride Highway. So it's just west of Enbridge

02:03:55.216 --> 02:03:57.855
here and And Eagle Mountain Storage. So it's this little area here.

02:03:59.670 --> 02:04:03.353
Here's a shot of the preliminary plat.

02:04:03.499 --> 02:04:05.187
So it's a 3-lot plat.

02:04:06.690 --> 02:04:10.103
Lot 1 is where the proposed school would be. It's a 6-acre lot.

02:04:10.667 --> 02:04:14.339
And then lots 2 and 3 would be, I'm guessing,

02:04:14.371 --> 02:04:15.949
just later phases of this development.

02:04:20.236 --> 02:04:23.381
Here's it again. So, go back

02:04:23.881 --> 02:04:26.946
to this. So, as I'm looking at this,

02:04:28.618 --> 02:04:32.033
our Transportation Master Plan, so this is Wagstaff Way, so this would be the north

02:04:32.533 --> 02:04:35.481
end of that preliminary plat, and then this road is there on the western edge,

02:04:36.015 --> 02:04:40.338
just some context. So we're looking at a future minor

02:04:40.838 --> 02:04:42.464
arterial and then a future collector road.

02:04:44.249 --> 02:04:47.726
So, this is, this plat that we're dealing with tonight,

02:04:49.254 --> 02:04:51.639
And then kind of gives you some context there is that you look at the

02:04:52.139 --> 02:04:55.593
Spring Run Plaza development, so you can kind of see where Wagstaff Way is

02:04:55.690 --> 02:04:59.159
looking to connect there. There will be a gap for the time being as

02:04:59.659 --> 02:05:03.386
those 2 roads develop, um, but eventually those will come together and form that connection.

02:05:05.701 --> 02:05:08.898
Uh, as we're reviewing it, there were 2 points that we want to bring up.

02:05:08.979 --> 02:05:12.776
So the first one is our code doesn't allow on preliminary plats

02:05:13.276 --> 02:05:16.031
to have lots front arterial and collector streets.

02:05:16.880 --> 02:05:20.406
Uh, in this case, I think staff's comfortable with allowing that, seeing as

02:05:20.906 --> 02:05:23.066
unless— like, we, we talked to the developer— unless they can find a way to

02:05:23.566 --> 02:05:26.383
do it, it's kind of tricky to do with a school and have them still

02:05:26.415 --> 02:05:29.476
function the way they need to. Uh, right now,

02:05:29.492 --> 02:05:32.408
the school's been proposing 2, um,

02:05:32.521 --> 02:05:35.533
ingress-egress points out of their property, and they're as far away from the intersection as

02:05:35.565 --> 02:05:39.139
possible. So we were— we think with the other 2

02:05:39.171 --> 02:05:43.279
lots, We're looking at maybe 1 or 2 or 3 additional

02:05:44.707 --> 02:05:48.174
points out onto those collector roads. So I feel like if it's— it's not

02:05:48.674 --> 02:05:51.753
necessarily an important standard to hold to in this case.

02:05:52.715 --> 02:05:56.054
And then the second one would be that western collector road.

02:05:57.129 --> 02:06:00.130
Go back. So this one right here, right now the developer is proposing it be

02:06:00.630 --> 02:06:03.291
named Gateway Park Boulevard.

02:06:03.885 --> 02:06:07.577
This will eventually connect up to Wild Blossom Boulevard in

02:06:08.077 --> 02:06:11.351
Saratoga Springs. With our recent code change that was approved,

02:06:12.218 --> 02:06:16.103
and just looking at it, I think staff feels that that name

02:06:16.603 --> 02:06:19.507
of Wild Blossom should probably continue just for coherency. Yes, it does,

02:06:20.728 --> 02:06:24.051
it will split the boundary between Saratoga Springs and Eagle Mountain, but I

02:06:24.551 --> 02:06:27.921
think it'll just create coherency on that road and make it easier to traverse

02:06:28.033 --> 02:06:30.570
and to find addresses and— Thank you.

02:06:31.470 --> 02:06:34.256
the cohesion between those 2. So those are the 2,

02:06:34.949 --> 02:06:39.669
um, conditions— that, that be renamed, and then if we're okay with not

02:06:40.103 --> 02:06:42.698
letting them have those access points onto the roads.

02:06:47.518 --> 02:06:50.371
I asked for this to be removed from the consent agenda because I want to

02:06:50.435 --> 02:06:53.353
talk about the name of the road.

02:06:53.885 --> 02:06:57.398
I get that for our code we've made it a priority

02:06:57.630 --> 02:07:00.995
for us to have roads contiguous have

02:07:01.011 --> 02:07:04.552
the same name. However, I think where

02:07:05.052 --> 02:07:08.142
I draw the line with that is where it runs into another city. Um,

02:07:08.959 --> 02:07:12.725
we have Woodhaven that is going to eventually

02:07:13.225 --> 02:07:16.843
connect to something over in Saratoga Springs, and we have Silver Lake Parkway

02:07:17.356 --> 02:07:20.513
that's going down to eventually connect with the new high school.

02:07:21.138 --> 02:07:25.276
And I don't see on any planet us Entertaining changing

02:07:25.308 --> 02:07:27.832
the name once it gets to a certain point,

02:07:28.507 --> 02:07:34.381
and Wild Blossom is a very design-specific

02:07:34.397 --> 02:07:37.786
name for the housing development

02:07:38.286 --> 02:07:41.659
that's there. And we have other streets

02:07:42.159 --> 02:07:47.080
in that general vicinity: Ranches Parkway, we have Spring

02:07:47.128 --> 02:07:51.233
Run, and I just think that. The project

02:07:51.282 --> 02:07:55.023
in this area will be better served with sticking to the overall

02:07:55.523 --> 02:07:56.503
name of Gateway Park Boulevard.

02:08:04.738 --> 02:08:07.472
One, I just had a question. I know I don't have a lot of say

02:08:07.972 --> 02:08:12.665
on this, but the driveway situation, I know staff said they didn't

02:08:13.165 --> 02:08:16.168
mind or that maybe it fit. I just wanted to raise the question what we've

