Well, and I think my, my point was with council, if we're not okay,

02:09:00.127 --> 02:09:02.987
would that be a solution? I just wanted to point that out, and, and I'm

02:09:03.084 --> 02:09:06.410
happy to let you address that if there is a concern.

02:09:06.458 --> 02:09:09.848
I don't know there is. I just wanted to bring that because

02:09:10.348 --> 02:09:12.300
it was addressed. Go ahead.

02:09:16.077 --> 02:09:18.833
Okay, is this not work— oh hey, it's working now. It wasn't working a week

02:09:19.333 --> 02:09:22.917
ago. Um, Scott Hazard, I'm, I'm the developer,

02:09:22.998 --> 02:09:26.389
one of the applicants. Uh, to answer your question, Mayor, these are

02:09:26.889 --> 02:09:30.380
not 6, 8, 10,000 square foot lots. This is a 6-acre parcel.

02:09:30.914 --> 02:09:33.632
Um, the intention you heard earlier is for a charter school site,

02:09:34.328 --> 02:09:37.759
so they'll have circulated egress that comes One off of Wagstaff

02:09:38.259 --> 02:09:41.882
Way and then one off of Gateway Park

02:09:41.898 --> 02:09:44.090
Boulevard, if you so see it that way.

02:09:46.815 --> 02:09:51.263
There really is no way to load this internally. If you recall the

02:09:51.763 --> 02:09:55.164
collaboration for Wagstaff Way and for Gateway Park

02:09:55.229 --> 02:09:58.628
Boulevard, these collectors and arterials that run through our

02:09:58.710 --> 02:10:01.927
600-acre master plan that we'll be bringing to you shortly, we're advancing this. Thank you.

02:10:02.072 --> 02:10:05.116
us accelerate it more quickly to meet the timeline of the charter school.

02:10:06.142 --> 02:10:08.962
Um, but this— all of those, uh,

02:10:09.346 --> 02:10:13.016
larger roadways were, were programmed

02:10:13.128 --> 02:10:16.525
and designed in collaboration with, uh, David Salazar and with the,

